    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for these. They're a decent start, but I think some of them are still a little bit too surface-level. I want to make sure we're really pushing the candidates.\n\nCan you try again? Give me five new questions, but this time, try to weave those core themes in even more clearly so I can be sure the candidate stays on topic. Even if it makes the questions a bit more dense, I'd rather have the themes (innovative, teamwork, synergy, growth-mindset, collaboration) baked into the core of the question so they can't dodge them. Just please try to keep them professionally worded!",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are five more deeply layered questions intentionally structured around your core themes. Describe a complex situation where your innovative thinking clashed with established protocols; how did you collaborate to achieve buy-in? Tell me about a project where achieving true teamwork required synthesizing very different departmental perspectives to unlock synergistic value. Can you give an example of when a required shift in perspective, demonstrating a strong growth-mindset, ultimately led to a highly innovative solution? Provide a specific instance where a lack of initial collaboration threatened a goal, and what specific actions you took to rebuild team synergy and drive forward. Finally, when faced with an ambiguous challenge, walk us through how your process blends iterative innovation with active teamwork to foster organizational growth-mindset.",
